RAM (Random Access Memory) and ROM (Read Only Memory) are two types of memory storage used in computers. 
RAM is a volatile memory, which means that it loses its contents when power is turned off. It is used to store data that is currently being used by the CPU. RAM is organized into memory cells, which are addressed by a unique identifier. Each memory cell can store a single bit of data. RAM is further divided into two types: Static RAM (SRAM) and Dynamic RAM (DRAM). SRAM is faster and more expensive than DRAM, but it consumes more power and has a lower density. DRAM is slower and less expensive than SRAM, but it is more power-efficient and has a higher density.
Here is an example C++ code snippet that illustrates the usage of RAM:
```c++
#include 
using namespace std;
int main() {
 int a = 5;
 int b = 10;
 int c = a + b;
 cout << "The sum of " << a << " and " << b << " is " << c << endl;
 return 0;
}
```
In this code, the variables `a`, `b`, and `c` are stored in RAM. The values of `a` and `b` are added together and stored in `c`, which is then printed to the console.
On the other hand, ROM is a non-volatile memory, which means that it retains its contents even when power is turned off. It is used to store data that is essential for the operation of the computer, such as the BIOS (Basic Input/Output System) and firmware. ROM is organized into memory cells, which are addressed by a unique identifier. Each memory cell can store a single bit of data. ROM is further divided into two types: Mask ROM and Programmable ROM. Mask ROM is created during the manufacturing process and cannot be modified. Programmable ROM can be programmed once with a special device, but cannot be changed afterwards.
Here is an example C++ code snippet that illustrates the usage of ROM:
```c++
#include 
using namespace std;
const int a = 5;
const int b = 10;
int main() {
 int c = a + b;
 cout << "The sum of " << a << " and " << b << " is " << c << endl;
 return 0;
}
```
In this code, the variables `a` and `b` are stored in ROM using the `const` keyword, which means that their values cannot be changed. The values of `a` and `b` are added together and stored in `c`, which is then printed to the console.
In terms of speed, RAM is faster than ROM because it can be accessed more quickly. In terms of capacity, RAM can hold more data than ROM because it is not limited by physical constraints. In terms of cost, RAM is more expensive than ROM because it is a more complex technology. In terms of durability, ROM is more durable than RAM because it is not affected by power loss or other external factors.
Overall, RAM and ROM are both important types of memory storage used in computers. RAM is used to store data that is currently being used by the CPU, while ROM is used to store data that is essential for the operation of the computer. RAM is faster and more expensive than ROM, but it is also more volatile. ROM is slower and less expensive than RAM, but it is also more durable.

